%% alt: Applications send every model call to an AI gateway, which checks identity and token quotas per team, routes each request to a model, falls back to another provider when one fails, and logs tokens and cost per team. Behind it, easy requests go to a hosted small model, hard ones to a hosted large model, failures to a second provider, and requests with private data to a self-hosted pool, where a serving engine with continuous batching and a paged KV cache runs the model on GPUs.
%% caption: Applications see one endpoint. Quotas, routing, fallback and cost tracking live in one place, in front of every model.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405
  classDef model fill:#e0e7ff,stroke:#4338ca,color:#14123d

  apps(["Apps and teams"])
  gw{{"AI gateway<br/>quotas · routing · fallback · logging"}}:::control
  logs[("Tokens and cost<br/>per team")]:::data
  small["Provider A<br/>small model"]:::model
  large["Provider A<br/>large model"]:::model
  backup["Provider B<br/>fallback model"]:::model
  pool["Self-hosted serving engine<br/>continuous batching · paged KV cache"]:::model
  gpus["GPU pool"]

  apps --> gw
  gw -.-> logs
  gw -- "easy" --> small
  gw -- "hard" --> large
  gw -. "on failure" .-> backup
  gw -- "private data" --> pool
  pool --> gpus
